From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:10:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Input: macsmc-input: set up wakeup before registering the SMC
 notifier

The wakeup source was initialised after the SMC notifier was
registered and was never torn down. Initialise it with
devm_device_init_wakeup() before the notifier, so that on removal the
notifier is unregistered (and its running callbacks drained) while the
input device and the wakeup source still exist.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/input/misc/macsmc-input.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/macsmc-input.c b/drivers/input/misc/macsmc-input.c
index e149b043fe..853dfa73b7 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/macsmc-input.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/macsmc-input.c
@@ -174,6 +174,15 @@ static int macsmc_input_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	input_sync(smcin->input);
 
+	/*
+	 * Register the wakeup cleanup before the notifier, so that removal
+	 * drains the notifier callbacks first, while both the input device
+	 * and the wakeup source are still alive.
+	 */
+	error = devm_device_init_wakeup(&pdev->dev);
+	if (error)
+		return error;
+
 	smcin->nb.notifier_call = macsmc_input_event;
 	error = blocking_notifier_chain_register(&smc->event_handlers, &smcin->nb);
 	if (error)
@@ -189,8 +198,6 @@ static int macsmc_input_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (error)
 		return error;
 
-	device_init_wakeup(&pdev->dev, true);
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
